The '''2023–24 Persian Gulf Pro League''' (formerly known as '''Iran Pro League''') was the 41st season of [[Persian Gulf Pro League|Iran's Football League]] and 23rd as [[Persian Gulf Pro League]] since its establishment in 2001.

==Teams==
===Promotion and relegation (pre-season)===
A total of sixteen teams contest the league, including fourteen sides from the [[2022–23 Persian Gulf Pro League|2022–23 season]] and two promoted from the [[2022–23 Azadegan League]]. This includes the two top teams from the Azadegan League.

